.TH SUB 1 "2026-08-31" "SUB Language" "SUB Language Manual"
.SH NAME
sub \- transpile a SUB program to another language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sub
.I input.sb
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sub
reads a SUB source file and writes the equivalent program in another
language. It does not build or run anything; the output is source, and
what you do with it is your business.
.PP
The interpreter,
.BR subi (1),
is the specification. Every target is held to producing the same output and
the same exit status as it does.
.SH TARGETS
If
.I target
is omitted, C is generated.
.SS Languages
.BR python " / " py ,
.BR javascript " / " js ,
.BR typescript " / " ts ,
.BR java ,
.BR c ,
.BR cpp " / " c++ ,
.BR rust " / " rs ,
.BR go " / " golang ,
.BR swift ,
.BR kotlin " / " kt ,
.BR ruby " / " rb ,
.BR assembly " / " asm ,
.BR css .
.SS Platforms
.BR android " (Java), " ios " (Swift), " web " (HTML/JS), " windows ", " macos ", " linux " (C)."
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print the target list and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUB_PATH
A colon-separated list of directories searched by
.B import
before the bundled standard library.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sub/stdlib
The standard library, found relative to the executable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The program was translated.
.TP
.B 1
The source did not compile.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
sub hello.sb python
sub hello.sb rust
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR subc (1),
.BR subi (1)
.SH BUGS
Report at https://github.com/subhobhai943/sub-lang/issues
